{
  "name": "Attack gate — repo and CI",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Repo and CI\n\nThis is the required check in front of merge. **Attack gate** runs first. A block or a hold never reaches the second matrix. Only an allow continues to **Implement gate**, which asks a different question set: what kind of change it is, and whether it is ready to ship. `delivery_risk` is not the attack `risk` score. They are separate calls.\n\n**Walk the examples:**\n\n1. A workflow permission change adds pull_request_target. The check fails.\n2. A dependency bump from a new maintainer is uncertain. A person reviews it. It does not reach Implement gate.\n3. A docs-only change is allowed, then Implement gate routes it to merge.\n4. A payments schema change is allowed through the attack gate, then held for design because the blast radius is wide.\n\nPOST /webhook/attack-change. Fail the check is exit-before-merge. Merge the change is the only path where `proceeded` is true.",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "a1030000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "How to read this",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -20
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "a1030000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Walk the examples",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        200,
        560
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "attack-change",
        "responseMode": "onReceived",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "a1030000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        200,
        760
      ],
      "webhookId": "attack-change"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "// Separate the untrusted request from facts the caller already verified.\n// The Attack gate reads state. It does not read the webhook envelope.\nconst item = $input.item.json;\nconst event = item.body && typeof item.body === 'object' && !Array.isArray(item.body) ? item.body : item;\nconst facts = event.facts && typeof event.facts === 'object' && !Array.isArray(event.facts) ? event.facts : {};\nconst request = typeof event.request === 'string' ? event.request : '';\nconst text = typeof event.text === 'string' && event.text !== '' ? event.text : request;\n\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    state: {\n      text,\n      request,\n      facts,\n      actor: event.actor ?? null,\n      action: event.action ?? null,\n      subject: event.subject ?? null,\n    },\n  },\n};\n"
      },
      "id": "a1030000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "Build state",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        480,
        640
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "state": "={{ JSON.stringify($json.state) }}",
        "questionSet": "custom",
        "questions": {
          "intent": {
            "type": "choice",
            "instructions": "What this event is, based on the facts in the state",
            "criteria": {
              "legitimate_ops": "Expected work by someone who should be doing it",
              "benign": "Ordinary request with no security impact",
              "account_takeover": "Signs that someone else is using an account, session, or recovery flow",
              "social_engineering": "A request to bypass, reset, or redirect a control or a payment",
              "supply_chain": "A change to build, dependency, CI, or release controls",
              "reconnaissance": "Probing for access, secrets, or weaknesses"
            }
          },
          "risk": {
            "type": "score",
            "instructions": "How much an automated action could change security, access, or data",
            "criteria": [
              "No security impact and easy to reverse",
              "Limited to one user or one record",
              "Touches authentication, secrets, or a shared control",
              "Bypasses a control, exposes data, or is hard to reverse"
            ]
          },
          "needs_human": {
            "type": "noul",
            "instructions": "A person should decide before any automated action"
          }
        },
        "rules": {
          "version": 1,
          "default_action": {
            "type": "escalate",
            "target": "human",
            "reason": "No matching rule",
            "gate": true
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "high_confidence": 0.85,
            "high_risk": 2
          },
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "hold-hostile",
              "description": "A confident hostile intent is blocked before any other route",
              "when": {
                "all": [
                  {
                    "question": "intent",
                    "in": [
                      "account_takeover",
                      "social_engineering",
                      "supply_chain",
                      "reconnaissance"
                    ],
                    "confidence_gte": "high_confidence"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "action": {
                "type": "block",
                "target": "security",
                "reason": "Hold {{answers.intent.choice}} before any automated action",
                "gate": true
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "hold-uncertain",
              "description": "High risk or a human-review signal goes to a person",
              "when": {
                "any": [
                  {
                    "question": "needs_human",
                    "gte": "high_confidence"
                  },
                  {
                    "question": "risk",
                    "gte": "high_risk"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "action": {
                "type": "escalate",
                "target": "human",
                "reason": "Risk or human-review signal crossed the threshold",
                "gate": true
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "allow-legitimate",
              "description": "Only a confident, low-risk, legitimate event can be automated",
              "when": {
                "all": [
                  {
                    "question": "intent",
                    "in": [
                      "legitimate_ops",
                      "benign"
                    ],
                    "confidence_gte": "high_confidence"
                  },
                  {
                    "question": "risk",
                    "lt": "high_risk"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "action": {
                "type": "allow",
                "target": "automation",
                "reason": "Allow {{answers.intent.choice}} below risk {{thresholds.high_risk}}",
                "gate": false
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "timeout": 60000,
          "includeFullAnswers": true,
          "failOnNoMatch": false
        }
      },
